(1388155, 173135, 34247, '<td valign="top">Thanks all. I''m quite happy with the shot, regardless of how it''d been placed, but I''m very happy as well with the fact that this had become my first ever (and probably only) top 10 in a challenge.<br/> <br/>If anyone wants to know, Jojo ran away the night after I took this shot, was missing for more than a day, and then the next morning was found licking himself on the backyard bench. Since then, he made tremendous improvements in terms of attitude towards the two new additions. By last night, they''re taking friendly swats at each other.<br/> <br/>Jojo was a street cat before we adopted him, and he clearly was reacting to other cats in a way that''s perhaps normal out in "the wilderness" of urban Colombo. Banjo and Spike, however, spent the first six months of their lives in the air-conditioned comfort of a diplomat''s house, and had just moved to ours a few weeks ago. Their reaction to Jojo was one of amusement. They''re smiling at him even as he was growling, spitting, hissing, etc. Although I hate anthropomorphizing, but they must have thought, based on the looks on their faces: "What''s his problem hissing and spitting? We''re friendly."<br/> <br/>Thanks :)</td>', 'Thanks all. I''m quite happy with the shot, regardless of how it''d been placed, but I''m very happy as well with the fact that this had become my first ever (and probably only) top 10 in a challenge. If anyone wants to know, Jojo ran away the night after I took this shot, was missing for more than a day, and then the next morning was found licking himself on the backyard bench. Since then, he made tremendous improvements in terms of attitude towards the two new additions. By last night, they''re taking friendly swats at each other. Jojo was a street cat before we adopted him, and he clearly was reacting to other cats in a way that''s perhaps normal out in "the wilderness" of urban Colombo. Banjo and Spike, however, spent the first six months of their lives in the air-conditioned comfort of a diplomat''s house, and had just moved to ours a few weeks ago. Their reaction to Jojo was one of amusement. They''re smiling at him even as he was growling, spitting, hissing, etc. Although I hate anthropomorphizing, but they must have thought, based on the looks on their faces: "What''s his problem hissing and spitting? We''re friendly." Thanks :)', '2005-05-16 04:54:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(1388160, 175598, 27845, '<td valign="top">I have <i>never</i> seen such an impressive use of perspective. So far, my favourite in that respect has been Julia Bailey''s ''Once upon a time'', but this is even better. I like the many concurring lines, the shapes that seem to fight each other, the shadows that split the larger surfaces into smaller shatters. The group of people give it the last touch of structured confusion.<br/>An excellent piece of art, which I cannot take my eyes off. Congratulations.</td>', 'I have never seen such an impressive use of perspective. So far, my favourite in that respect has been Julia Bailey''s ''Once upon a time'', but this is even better. I like the many concurring lines, the shapes that seem to fight each other, the shadows that split the larger surfaces into smaller shatters. The group of people give it the last touch of structured confusion.An excellent piece of art, which I cannot take my eyes off. Congratulations.', '2005-05-16 05:14:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(1388189, 175598, 35044, '<td valign="top">The fact that I can continue looking at this and see more and more is testament to its great quality.  The only reason for it not coming higher is probably the need to look at this closely: perhaps too much to ask in a competition of this style.  Great image.</td>', 'The fact that I can continue looking at this and see more and more is testament to its great quality.  The only reason for it not coming higher is probably the need to look at this closely: perhaps too much to ask in a competition of this style.  Great image.', '2005-05-16 05:54:47.000000', NULL, 0),
