(1407810, 175806, 34154, '<td valign="top">i really like this shot, and i too am surprised that it didnt score higher.  maybe if there was either no curtain or more on both sides of the frame and the rest of her hand. but i love the feeling of this, the colors are soothing</td>', 'i really like this shot, and i too am surprised that it didnt score higher.  maybe if there was either no curtain or more on both sides of the frame and the rest of her hand. but i love the feeling of this, the colors are soothing', '2005-05-24 02:52:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(1427838, 175525, 38655, '<td valign="top">wow this is a pretty cool shot, the model is pretty :P lol but yeah can''t really find anything to nag you about so I''m going to say a job well done :)</td>', 'wow this is a pretty cool shot, the model is pretty :P lol but yeah can''t really find anything to nag you about so I''m going to say a job well done :)', '2005-06-01 23:31:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(1428505, 175718, 38001, '<td valign="top">it''s creative picture. Nice, man<br/></td>', 'it''s creative picture. Nice, man', '2005-06-02 04:20:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(1437568, 174408, 25655, '<td valign="top">No comments? on a challenge pic? how bizzare!!!<br/> <br/>Great photo. I love the details of the fish and I like your DOF and spotlight. <br/>A couple of suggestions I would have (if I may..) are try (in photoshop) to lower the saturation of the background a little. It''s tad too red. Such lovely fish should stand out a lot more in the photo.<br/>Also, try re-shooting with your spotlight coming from a lot higher then it is right now, so that the shadow of the fish will be lost in the bottom part of the anyway dark background.<br/> <br/>Still, I think it''s a crime not having any comments on this one. I think it''s a great take on that challenge and I''m sorry I didn''t get to vote then.</td>', 'No comments? on a challenge pic? how bizzare!!! Great photo. I love the details of the fish and I like your DOF and spotlight. A couple of suggestions I would have (if I may..) are try (in photoshop) to lower the saturation of the background a little. It''s tad too red. Such lovely fish should stand out a lot more in the photo.Also, try re-shooting with your spotlight coming from a lot higher then it is right now, so that the shadow of the fish will be lost in the bottom part of the anyway dark background. Still, I think it''s a crime not having any comments on this one. I think it''s a great take on that challenge and I''m sorry I didn''t get to vote then.', '2005-06-06 19:36:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(1447606, 175408, 11800, '<td valign="top">I saw the thread about negative, umm.. constructive comments so, since I''m free for a moment, I thought I''d stop by. I picked this one because of the score.<br/>The score mostly reflects, to me, a lot of people thinking you didn''t meet the challenge enough. To get that many 4''s on a picture that is in focus and not controversial usually means it lacks a strong connection to the challenge discription.<br/>The lighting looks harsh with sharp shadows on the main flower and most of the other flowers are obscured. The frame is cluttered with things that detract from the beauty of the one bloom. A closer crop would have eliminated all of that. My suggestion is to look at the scene thru the viewfinder and ask yourself if something supports the idea you are trying to capture. If it isn''t supporting it, it shouldn''t be in the frame.</td>', 'I saw the thread about negative, umm.. constructive comments so, since I''m free for a moment, I thought I''d stop by. I picked this one because of the score.The score mostly reflects, to me, a lot of people thinking you didn''t meet the challenge enough. To get that many 4''s on a picture that is in focus and not controversial usually means it lacks a strong connection to the challenge discription.The lighting looks harsh with sharp shadows on the main flower and most of the other flowers are obscured. The frame is cluttered with things that detract from the beauty of the one bloom. A closer crop would have eliminated all of that. My suggestion is to look at the scene thru the viewfinder and ask yourself if something supports the idea you are trying to capture. If it isn''t supporting it, it shouldn''t be in the frame.', '2005-06-11 13:56:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(1448313, 175408, 15711, '<td valign="top">Excellent macro.  Lovely choice of flower with the varigation of the color.  Really like this one.</td>', 'Excellent macro.  Lovely choice of flower with the varigation of the color.  Really like this one.', '2005-06-11 22:42:36.000000', NULL, 0),
